    "m2_prompt_trader_proposal_original": "**Action**: Hold\n\n**Reasoning**: The evidence is genuinely balanced with no decisive edge for either direction. Technically, JPM sits in a bullish stack above the 10-day EMA, 50-day SMA, and 200-day SMA, but momentum is stalling (negative MACD histogram for three weeks, lower-high pattern since May 17, -1.32% 5-day return). The $186 triple-confluence support held and produced a bounce, but on below-average volume. Fundamentally, the picture is unverifiable \u2014 the -$154.2B operating cash flow and 8.2% equity-to-assets ratio could reflect either loan growth (bullish) or trading losses (bearish), and sentiment/news/macro data are unavailable in this historical window. Per the research plan, maintain current positions at benchmark weight, respect $186 as the hard risk line, and treat $195-$196 as the upside trigger. Do not add aggressively given stalled momentum and unquantified macro risk.\n\n**Entry Price**: 190.83\n\n**Stop Loss**: 186.0\n\n**Position Sizing**: Neutral benchmark-weight allocation; do not concentrate beyond normal portfolio weight\n\nFINAL TRANSACTION PROPOSAL: **HOLD**",
